<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 71 0 R/T(Wait-die: older requester may wait for younger holder; younger requester aborts if it requests a lock held by older. Wound-wait: older requester aborts \(wounds\) younger holder; younger requester waits for older. Starvation can occur through repeated victimization. FIFO queues, bounded retries and retry aging \(increasing priority after each retry\) reduce risk, but do not prove fairness under every workload. )/E(Wait-die: older requester may wait for younger holder; younger requester aborts if it requests a lock held by older. Wound-wait: older requester aborts \(wounds\) younger holder; younger requester waits for older. Starvation can occur through repeated victimization. FIFO queues, bounded retries and retry aging \(increasing priority after each retry\) reduce risk, but do not prove fairness under every workload. )/Pg 14 0 R/K[5]>>
