284 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 72 0 R/T(Assume log generation1,000 records/s, scan+redo cost 0.02 ms/record, undo cost 0.01 ms/record, fixed startup 2 seconds. At a 285-second checkpoint interval, up to 285,000 records may need examination: 2 + \(285,000\3270.02 ms\)/1,000 = 7.7 seconds for scan/redo, plus undo. This simplified estimate is below 35 seconds, but leaves less margin if actual log rate or costs rise. A 20-second interval retains at most 20,000 records, giving 2 + 0.4 = 2.4 seconds before undo overhead. Checkpoint interval must be selected from measured worst-case log rate and replay cost, not this estimate alone. )/E(Assume log generation1,000 records/s, scan+redo cost 0.02 ms/record, undo cost 0.01 ms/record, fixed startup 2 seconds. At a 285-second checkpoint interval, up to 285,000 records may need examination: 2 + \(285,000\3270.02 ms\)/1,000 = 7.7 seconds for scan/redo, plus undo. This simplified estimate is below 35 seconds, but leaves less margin if actual log rate or costs rise. A 20-second interval retains at most 20,000 records, giving 2 + 0.4 = 2.4 seconds before undo overhead. Checkpoint interval must be selected from measured worst-case log rate and replay cost, not this estimate alone. )/Pg 15 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

