417 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 75 0 R/T(The changed rule concentrates 81% of allocations on one canal pool and adds a per-farm daily ceiling. The previous assumption that resource accesses are dispersed or that the transaction touches only a fixed pair of canal records is no longer sufficient. The dominant pool receives 54.27 requests/s at 67 requests/s total. With 20 ms exclusive service, its theoretical single-record capacity is 50 requests/s, so its utilization is 108.5% and backlog grows during sustained input. The 35-second restart deadline must be checked against retained log volume. At 1,000 log records/s, a 285-second interval retains 285,000 records; under the stated 0.02 ms/record replay and 2-second startup model this is 7.7 seconds, below 35 seconds. However, it has less margin than a 20-second interval \(20,000 records; 2.4 seconds\). These are model estimates, not guarantees. )/E(The changed rule concentrates 81% of allocations on one canal pool and adds a per-farm daily ceiling. The previous assumption that resource accesses are dispersed or that the transaction touches only a fixed pair of canal records is no longer sufficient. The dominant pool receives 54.27 requests/s at 67 requests/s total. With 20 ms exclusive service, its theoretical single-record capacity is 50 requests/s, so its utilization is 108.5% and backlog grows during sustained input. The 35-second restart deadline must be checked against retained log volume. At 1,000 log records/s, a 285-second interval retains 285,000 records; under the stated 0.02 ms/record replay and 2-second startup model this is 7.7 seconds, below 35 seconds. However, it has less margin than a 20-second interval \(20,000 records; 2.4 seconds\). These are model estimates, not guarantees. )/Pg 18 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

418 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 75 0 R/T(Decision: MODIFY, not retain unchanged and not replace the core concurrency protocol. Keep strict 2PL + WAL, but extend the lock scope to include \(1\) source canal pool, \(2\) destination canal pool, \(3\) farm_id + service_date usage row, and \(4\) any predicate/index range used to locate the farm's daily allocations. Acquire all lock keys in one deterministic global order. Validate remaining farm allowance and source pool balance after locks are held, then debit/credit and increment daily farm usage in the same transaction. )/E(Decision: MODIFY, not retain unchanged and not replace the core concurrency protocol. Keep strict 2PL + WAL, but extend the lock scope to include \(1\) source canal pool, \(2\) destination canal pool, \(3\) farm_id + service_date usage row, and \(4\) any predicate/index range used to locate the farm's daily allocations. Acquire all lock keys in one deterministic global order. Validate remaining farm allowance and source pool balance after locks are held, then debit/credit and increment daily farm usage in the same transaction. )/Pg 18 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

419 0 obj
