468 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 76 0 R/E(The measured model results in Task 9 show that hotspot mean and p95 latency rise with burst size, while uniform accesses distribute work. The strict-2PL schedule is conflict-serializable and strict because conflicting writes are ordered and X locks are held to transaction end. The per-farm ceiling requires a new guarded predicate; it is not proven by the token-only tests. )/Pg 19 0 R/K[31]>>
endobj

469 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 76 0 R/E(Restart calculation: at 1,000 records/s, 20 seconds retains 20,000 records. At 0.02 ms/record, replay scan/redo costs 0.4 seconds; adding 2 seconds fixed startup gives 2.4 seconds before undo and checkpoint overhead. The 285-second policy retains 285,000 records and costs 7.7 seconds by the same model. Both are below 35 seconds under these assumptions, but 20 seconds provides more headroom. The final selection is based on the stated deadline and model, not on a protocol label. )/Pg 19 0 R/K[32]>>
