780 0 obj
<</Title(No-control negative reference: two transactionsboth read source balance 10, each approves 7, and both write 3. The final source balance is 3 rather than a valid-4orone approved transfer; the system has overspent by 4 tokens. Serial execution permits only one transfer. S2PLmakesthe second transaction read the first transaction's committed balance and reject. TO aborts the transaction whosetimestamp order cannot be maintained.)/Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Parent 735 0 R/Next 781 0 R>>
endobj

781 0 obj
<</Title(Failure coverage: serial execution is the referencecorrectness schedule; S2PL excludes conflicting lost updates and, when strict, dirty dependencies; TO excludestimestamp-order violations. Neither TO nor locking automatically validates a farm-specific daily ceiling unless that predicateisincluded in the transaction's protected read/write set.)/Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Parent 735 0 R/Prev 780 0 R>>
endobj

782 0 obj
<</Title(Transaction form)/Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Parent 736 0 R/Next 789 0 R>>
endobj

783 0 obj
<</Title(Anomalies: Lost update \205 T1 and T2 both read A=10 and overwrite A with 4 and 3; one debit disappears. Dirty read \205 T2 reads T1's uncommitted A=3, then T1 aborts. Repeated/non-repeatable read \205 T1 reads A=10, T2 commits a transfer, and T1 reads A=6. Mixed summary \205 report reads A before a transfer and B after it, showing a total that never existed. Phantom \205 a report queries all farms whose daily use exceeds a threshold; another transaction inserts a qualifying allocation row, so the second query returns an extra row.)/Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Parent 736 0 R/Prev 789 0 R>>
endobj

