834 0 obj
<</Title(Recoverable means a reader commits only after the transaction it read from commits. ACA \(avoids cascading aborts\) means transactions read only committed values. Strict schedules additionally prohibit reading or writing an item written by an uncommitted transaction. A single aborted allocation can invalidate later decisions if T2 reads T1's temporary)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 792 0 R/Prev 833 0 R/Next 818 0 R>>
endobj

835 0 obj
<</Title(Upgradetrace: T1 obtains S\(A\) and reads A.T2 also obtains S\(A\). T1 requests upgrade to X\(A\),but must wait for T2's S\(A\) torelease. If T2 also requests upgrade,both wait: a conversion deadlock. Avoid by acquiringX\(A\) initially when an updateisknown, or use a single-upgrader queue.)/Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Parent 806 0 R/Prev 819 0 R/First 850 0 R/Last 851 0 R/Count -2/Next 836 0 R>>
endobj

836 0 obj
<</Title<>/Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Parent 806 0 R/Prev 835 0 R/Next 820 0 R>>
endobj

837 0 obj
<</Title<>/Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Parent 821 0 R/Next 852 0 R>>
endobj

838 0 obj
<</Title(TO is deadlock-free because transactions do not waitfor data locks; conflicts cause aborts. However, repeated late arrivals or hot-item conflicts can cause repeated aborts and starvation. Strict TO needs an additional rule to delay access to uncommitted writes.)/Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Parent 821 0 R/Prev 852 0 R>>
endobj

