endobj

841 0 obj
<</Title(The followingare computed from the deterministic open-loop model described above. Throughput is completed deliveriesdivided by elapsed time from time zero to the last completion. Mean and nearest-rank p95 include waiting from arrival.The lock-wait column is the mean time waiting for the selected pool; admission queueing is zero because this modelhasno separate admission cap.)/Dest[16 0 R/Fit]/Parent 822 0 R/First 857 0 R/Last 858 0 R/Count -3/Next 842 0 R>>
endobj

842 0 obj
<</Title(Retry/abort and wait-for-cycle interpretation: the lock schedule itself waits rather than aborting on ordinaryconflicts. Canonical lock ordering yields zero lock-order deadlock cycles in this model. Basic TO has no waits; a conservative overlap-based retry indicator can be calculated from the same request stream, but it is not a measured SQL-engine abort count. Recovery work is modeled as at most log-rate \327 checkpoint interval records; it is not an observed disk replay count.)/Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Parent 822 0 R/Prev 841 0 R/First 859 0 R/Last 859 0 R/Count -1>>
endobj

843 0 obj
<</Title(The simulator reflects this: the hotspot workload has higher mean and tail latency and lower completed throughput for large bursts. This is not proof that TO or any lock implementation will have the same numbers; real performance depends on disk, CPU, worker count, lock manager, batching and transaction duration. The model intentionally gives the same operation cost and arrival stream to the compared workload modes.)/Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Parent 807 0 R/Prev 823 0 R/Next 824 0 R>>
endobj

844 0 obj
<</Title(On lock conflict, queue; on a detected deadlock, abort a selected victim and retry with bounded backoff/aging.)/Dest[18 0 R/Fit]/Parent 808 0 R/Prev 825 0 R/Next 860 0 R>>
endobj

845 0 obj
<</Title(Farm daily ceiling is not covered by the token-only implementation; add a farm_id + service_date usage record and validate/update it in the same transaction.)/Dest[18 0 R/Fit]/Parent 808 0 R/Prev 861 0 R/Next 826 0 R>>
endobj

846 0 obj
<</Title(Option)/Dest[18 0 R/Fit]/Parent 827 0 R/Next 862 0 R>>
endobj

847 0 obj
<</Title(Cost / limitation)/Dest[18 0 R/Fit]/Parent 827 0 R/Prev 862 0 R>>
endobj

848 0 obj
<</Title(Strict?)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 833 0 R/Next 849 0 R>>
endobj

849 0 obj
<</Title(Reason)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 833 0 R/Prev 848 0 R>>
endobj

850 0 obj
<</Title(Rule)/Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Parent 835 0 R/Next 851 0 R>>
endobj

851 0 obj
<</Title(RiverGate effect)/Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Parent 835 0 R/Prev 850 0 R>>
endobj

852 0 obj
<</Title(Thomas' rule: if T's blind write to a dispatch markerhas TS\(T\) < WTS\(marker\), it is obsolete and can be ignored because a newer write already superseded it. A water-token debit is conditional on the current source allowance; silently ignoring it would falsely report success. Thetransaction must validate the predicate and abort/retry if its read/write order is obsolete.)/Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Parent 821 0 R/Prev 837 0 R/Next 838 0 R>>
endobj

853 0 obj
<</Title(WAL records and checkpoint)/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Parent 839 0 R/First 863 0 R/Last 864 0 R/Count -6/Next 865 0 R>>
endobj

854 0 obj
<</Title(Restart-time model)/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Parent 839 0 R/Prev 866 0 R/First 867 0 R/Last 867 0 R/Count -1>>
endobj

855 0 obj
<</Title(The experiment below is a reproducible scheduling model. Eachdelivery uses an exclusive lock on its selected canal pool for 20 ms. It records lock waiting and response time from arrival. It does not simulate a full SQL engine, real disk I/O, farm-ceiling checks or a production thread scheduler.)/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Parent 840 0 R/Next 868 0 R>>
endobj

856 0 obj
<</Title(Domain gap: the token-only test does not enforce a per-farm daily ceiling. A correct extension must lock or serializably validate the farm/day usage row and the canal pool row, then atomically update both.)/Dest[16 0 R/Fit]/Parent 840 0 R/Prev 869 0 R>>
endobj

857 0 obj
<</Title(Mean latency ms)/Dest[16 0 R/Fit]/Parent 841 0 R/Next 870 0 R>>
endobj

858 0 obj
<</Title(Maxlock wait ms)/Dest[16 0 R/Fit]/Parent 841 0 R/Prev 870 0 R>>
endobj

859 0 obj
<</Title(Max retained records at 1,000 records/s)/Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Parent 842 0 R>>
endobj

860 0 obj
<</Title(Use a clean checkpoint every 20 seconds as the conservative initial policy under the stated log model; validate the worst-case restart time with actual log and replay measurements.)/Dest[18 0 R/Fit]/Parent 808 0 R/Prev 844 0 R/Next 861 0 R>>
endobj

861 0 obj
<</Title(Do not claim measured production throughput. Use Task 9's model output only as evidence about the stated 20 ms exclusive-service model.)/Dest[18 0 R/Fit]/Parent 808 0 R/Prev 860 0 R/Next 845 0 R>>
endobj

862 0 obj
<</Title(Benefit)/Dest[18 0 R/Fit]/Parent 827 0 R/Prev 846 0 R/Next 847 0 R>>
endobj

863 0 obj
<</Title(<START T1>)/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Parent 853 0 R/Next 871 0 R>>
endobj

864 0 obj
<</Title(Clean checkpoint means all transactions have finished, all dirty pages are flushed, and the checkpoint-end record is durable. It provides a known restart boundary.)/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Parent 853 0 R/Prev 872 0 R>>
endobj

865 0 obj
<</Title(Deferred versus immediate update)/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Parent 839 0 R/Prev 853 0 R/First 873 0 R/Last 873 0 R/Count -1/Next 866 0 R>>
endobj

866 0 obj
<</Title(Worked crash trace \(defined example\))/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Parent 839 0 R/Prev 865 0 R/First 874 0 R/Last 875 0 R/Count -3/Next 854 0 R>>
endobj

867 0 obj
<</Title(Assume log generation1,000 records/s, scan+redo cost 0.02 ms/record, undo cost 0.01 ms/record, fixed startup 2 seconds. At a 285-second checkpoint interval, up to 285,000 records may need examination: 2 + \(285,000\3270.02 ms\)/1,000 = 7.7 seconds for scan/redo, plus undo. This simplified estimate is below 35 seconds, but leaves less margin if actual log rate or costs rise. A 20-second interval retains at most 20,000 records, giving 2 + 0.4 = 2.4 seconds before undo overhead. Checkpoint interval must be selected from measured worst-case log rate and replay cost, not this estimate alone.)/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Parent 854 0 R>>
endobj

868 0 obj
<</Title(Run the same seed and request list for every candidate; record seed, burst size, workload mode, service time and canal count.)/Dest[16 0 R/Fit]/Parent 840 0 R/Prev 855 0 R/Next 876 0 R>>
endobj

869 0 obj
<</Title(Crash-test immediate update by undoing losers and redoing winners; crash-test deferred update by redoing winners only. Compare recovered balances with the committed-history reference.)/Dest[16 0 R/Fit]/Parent 840 0 R/Prev 877 0 R/Next 856 0 R>>
endobj

870 0 obj
<</Title(Meanlock wait ms)/Dest[16 0 R/Fit]/Parent 841 0 R/Prev 857 0 R/Next 858 0 R>>
endobj

871 0 obj
<</Title(<COMMIT T1>)/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Parent 853 0 R/Prev 863 0 R/Next 878 0 R>>
endobj

872 0 obj
<</Title(Undo uses old values for uncommitted transactions; redo uses new values for committed transactions. Request IDs are logged with the movement.)/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Parent 853 0 R/Prev 879 0 R/Next 864 0 R>>
endobj

873 0 obj
<</Title(Crash handling)/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Parent 865 0 R>>
endobj

874 0 obj
<</Title<>/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Parent 866 0 R/First 880 0 R/Last 881 0 R/Count -2/Next 882 0 R>>
endobj

875 0 obj
<</Title(Shadow paging writes changed pages elsewhere and atomically switches the root pointer at commit. It avoids log undo/redo but repeated small canal-pool changes cause page copying, fragmentation and expensive root/page maintenance; it is less attractive for frequent small updates.)/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Parent 866 0 R/Prev 882 0 R>>
endobj

876 0 obj
<</Title(After each committed movement, assert sum\(balances\) is unchanged, no balance is negative, and each request ID appears once.)/Dest[16 0 R/Fit]/Parent 840 0 R/Prev 868 0 R/Next 883 0 R>>
endobj

877 0 obj
<</Title<>/Dest[16 0 R/Fit]/Parent 840 0 R/Prev 883 0 R/Next 869 0 R>>
endobj

878 0 obj
<</Title(Write-ahead logging: before a changed data page is written, its log record must be durable.)/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Parent 853 0 R/Prev 871 0 R/Next 879 0 R>>
endobj

879 0 obj
<</Title(Commit-force: before success is returned, the commit record \(and all earlier log records for that transaction\) must be forced to stable storage.)/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Parent 853 0 R/Prev 878 0 R/Next 872 0 R>>
endobj

